2025-10-11 11:21:32 [simon@midnightblue] this 🏛️ is returning 3 for stringWidth?
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] Yes, the `stringWidth` function is returning 3 for "🏛️" because it's counting the emoji as 2
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] columns (which is correct for wide characters), but there's an issue with how the variation
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] selector `\uFE0F` is being handled.
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] The emoji "🏛️" consists of:
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] - U+1F3DB (Classical Building) - wide character (2 columns)
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] - U+FE0F (Variation Selector-16) - zero width
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] The current implementation counts the variation selector as 1 column instead of 0, giving a total
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] of 3 instead of 2.
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] You could fix this by modifying the `isWide` function to exclude variation selectors:
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] function isWide(cp: number): boolean {
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat]     if (cp === 0xFE0F) return false; // Variation Selector-16 is zero width
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat]     return WideRanges.some(([start, end]) => cp >= start && cp <= end);
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] }
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] Or modify `stringWidth` to handle variation selectors specifically:
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] 
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] function stringWidth(text: string): number {
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat]     let w = 0;
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat]     for (const ch of text) {
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat]         const codePoint = ch.codePointAt(0) ?? 0;
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat]         if (codePoint === 0xFE0F) continue; // Skip variation selectors
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat]         w += isWide(codePoint) ? 2 : 1;
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat]     }
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat]     return w;
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] }
2025-10-11 11:22:25 [deepseek-chat] 
