2025-10-28 12:03:50 [simon@midnightblue] what is tools interface proper name?
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] The proper name for the tools interface is Function Calling (or sometimes Tool
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] Use).
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] In OpenAI's API, it's specifically called the Functions feature or Function Calling
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] API. Other providers use similar terminology:
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] - OpenAI: "Functions" / "Function Calling"
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Anthropic: "Tool Use"
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Google Gemini: "Function Calling"
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] - DeepSeek: "Tool Call"
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] In your code, you're implementing it via the `rohaTools` array and handling responses with
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] `processToolCalls()`. The standard pattern involves:
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] 1. Defining tools/functions in the request payload
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] 2. Model returns `tool_calls` in the response
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] 3. Execute the called function
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] 4. Return results back to the model in a new message
2025-10-28 12:03:57 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:04:31 [simon@midnightblue] does anthropic support tools?
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] Yes, Anthropic supports tools. In your code, you're already implementing it in the
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] `anthropicTools()` function around line 2100.
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] Anthropic calls it Tool Use (their terminology). Key details:
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] - API support: Yes, fully supported
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Format: Tools are defined in the request and the model returns `tool_use` blocks in
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] responses
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] - Your implementation:
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5]   - `anthropicTools(payload)` converts your standard tool format to Anthropic's `input_schema`
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] format
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5]   - `anthropicMessages()` handles `toolcalls` from your payload and maps them to Anthropic's
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] `tooluse` format
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5]   - Response parsing extracts `tool_use` content and maps back to OpenAI-compatible format
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] The mapping happens around line 2250 where tool results are converted:
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] const tool_use = item.tool_calls.map(call => ({
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	type: "tool_use",
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	id: call.id,
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	name: call.function.name,
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 	input: JSON.parse(call.function.arguments || "{}")
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] }));
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] So yes—Anthropic Claude models fully support tool use, and your code already handles it.
2025-10-28 12:04:38 [claude-haiku-4-5] 
